  "worked_solution": "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(-1,4)\\cup (6,7)$ is open. It consists of two parts, where the boundary points are $-1$, $4$, $6$, and $7.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not open because:\n\n- $(-2,1]\\cup [3,9)$ has four boundary points $-2$, $1$, $3$, and $9$, and the points $1$ and $3$ lie in the set.\n\n- $[4,6)\\cup (9,11)$ has four boundary points $4$, $6$, $9$, and $11$, and the point $4$ lies in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\".",
